{
  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "Where events take place: ser",
      "body": "Location normally uses *estar*, but the location of an **event** uses *ser*: *La fiesta es en mi casa.* (The party is at my house.) *¿Dónde es el concierto?* *La boda fue en una iglesia.* Compare: *Mi casa está en el centro.* (a place) vs. *La reunión es en el centro.* (an event)."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Estar de…",
      "body": "*Estar de* + noun describes a temporary role or situation: *estar de vacaciones* (on vacation), *estar de viaje* (traveling), *estar de pie* (standing), *estar de rodillas* (kneeling), *estar de acuerdo*, *estar de buen / mal humor* (in a good / bad mood), *estar de moda* (in fashion), *estar de luto* (in mourning). And *estar de* + job for a temporary position: *Está de mesero este verano.* (He's working as a waiter this summer.)"
    },
    {
